From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 22:45:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] drm/meson: dw-hdmi: end the register map at the DWC block

The regmap dw-hdmi reaches the controller through claims registers up to
0x10000, past the 64 KiB block the HDMI TX node maps. The DWC registers
are 0x0000 to 0x7fff; TOP, from 0x8000 on the direct layout, has its own
accessors. Reading the map through debugfs on GXLX2, which takes G12A's
direct access, reads 0x10000 off the end: an oops in
dw_hdmi_g12a_dwc_read() with the regmap lock held and interrupts off,
and the next reader hard-locks the CPU.

End the map at 0x7fff.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
diff -urN a/drivers/gpu/drm/meson/meson_dw_hdmi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/meson/meson_dw_hdmi.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/meson/meson_dw_hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/meson/meson_dw_hdmi.c
@@ -569,7 +569,7 @@
 	.val_bits = 8,
 	.reg_read = meson_dw_hdmi_reg_read,
 	.reg_write = meson_dw_hdmi_reg_write,
-	.max_register = 0x10000,
+	.max_register = 0x7fff,
 	.fast_io = true,
 };
 
